  "engineered_computation.ponder.tag.era1": "Analogue Era",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tag.era1.description": "Punch cards, Tube Stations and the Tabulator Machine",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.header": "Setting up a Tabulator Machine",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.text_1": "Build the Tabulator Machine from Analogue Casings in this shape",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.text_2": "Right-click the front with the Assembly Wrench to form it",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.text_3": "Place a Tube Station against an inventory, with its hatch facing it",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.text_4": "Connect the stations to the Tabulator Machine with Pneumatic Tubes",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.text_5": "Requested items are sent to a Receiving Station",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.text_6": "Place a Teletype Terminal against a Receiving Station to request items from the network",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.text_7": "To punch a Catalogue Card with a station's location, right-click the Tube Station with it",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.text_8": "File punched cards in a Card Deck, then place the deck in the Tabulator Machine",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_setup.text_9": "The station's items can now be requested from the Teletype Terminal",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.header": "Sending items between stations",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.text_1": "A tube network can have several Receiving Stations",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.text_2": "To add a window to a tube, sneak while right-clicking it with an empty hand",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.text_3": "To hide a tube, sneak while placing a block on it to cover it",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.text_4": "Right-click a Receiving Station to name it",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.text_5": "Each Receiving Station can have its own Teletype Terminal",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.text_6": "To send items to another Receiving Station, choose it under To: on the Teletype Terminal's request slip",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.text_7": "Without a Pressurizer, each carrier holds %1$s items",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.text_8": "A Pressurizer anywhere on the network raises it to high pressure while it has fuel",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_usage.text_9": "At high pressure, each carrier holds %1$s items",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_autosmelting.header": "Smelting On Demand using the tube network",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_autosmelting.text_1": "Observing Autotubes can run a furnace from the tube network",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_autosmelting.text_2": "Right-click a Tube Station to set it to take new items",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_autosmelting.text_3": "Set to eject, a Receiving Station puts what it receives into the inventory in front of it",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_autosmelting.text_4": "An Observing Autotube pulls items whenever the inventory at its intake changes",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_autosmelting.text_5": "Before items are sent to it, sneak while right-clicking it to set how many it pulls at once",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_autosmelting.text_6": "A second Observing Autotube sends each smelted item to a Tube Station holding it, or one that takes new items",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_autosmelting.text_7": "Request the raw iron to the Melter from the Teletype Terminal",
  "engineered_computation.ponder.tabulator_autosmelting.text_8": "Over time, each iron ingot is sent back to the results station",
